#ifndef WXL_SEAM
#error "define WXL_SEAM(domain, name, symbol, ret, conv, params) before including client.def"
#endif

// Takes the client apart: the glue, the add-ons, the client databases, the sound, the script
// context, the console, in that order. One caller, on the way out of the main function, while
// everything a mod might still hold is alive and the process is not yet being torn down. That
// is the last moment at which a mod can be told anything, and it is where the shutdown stage
// and the unload run.
//
// A file-level static, so the compiler was free to give it a convention of its own -- but it
// takes no arguments and returns nothing, so there is no argument to misread and no stack to
// clean either way, and a cdecl detour is correct whatever the compiler chose. This is the
// only kind of internal-linkage static a row may declare without disassembling it first.
//
// Before does the work. After is where the runtime would be if there were anything left to do
// after a mod's last line has run, and there is not.
WXL_SEAM(Client, Destroy, "WowClientDestroy", void, cdecl, ())
